--- !u!114 &1406261143
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1406261139}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "V0.6\n\nBug Fixes\n1. Fixed a bug where the user was able to control the
    cube while the level complete panel was enabled. \n\n2. Fixed a bug where the
    user was able to press ESC to open the pause menu while the level complete and
    the game over panel was enabled.\n\n3. Fixed a bug that caused the game to freeze
    when the user pressed the ESC button to open the pause menu.\n\n4. Fixed a bug
    that caused the player's rotation to break while the cube passed a certain amount
    of speed.\n\nChanges\n1. Upgraded the Unity version, which will bring a lot of
    crash fixes and optimizations.\n\n2. Improved collision detection.\n\n3. Reworked
    the UI and optimized the code from the level complete screen.\n\n4. Reworked
    the UI and optimized the code from the pause menu.\n\n5. Reduced the slipperiness
    of the character.\n\n6. The game will take less space than before due to the
    new compression method and the optimization in the code.\n\n7. Smoothed graphics
    in general. No more glitchy stuff.\n\nNew\n1. Added a 3D text above the invisible
    end trigger (finish line) to inform the player that they are about to finish
    the level.\n\n2. Added a text to the main menu to remind the user that they can
    reset their progress in case they need to.\n\n\nV0.5\n\nBug Fixes\n1. Fixed a
    bug that caused the shadows to display in the wrong position.\n\n2. Fixed a bug
    that caused the game to restart while the level complete UI shows up. That would
    happen if the player fell off the platform.\n\nChanges\n1. Changed the sky again.\n\n2.
    Changed the restart delay from 1 second to 20 seconds.\n\n3. Updated the how-to-play
    page.\n\nNew\n1. Added a patch notes button in the main menu that opens a page
    and shows the latest and older changes. \n\n2. Added a level selector menu.\n\n3.
    Added a save file system that saves the player's progress localy.\n\n4. Added
    a way to manually reset your progress.\n\n5. Added animation of the clouds.\n\n6.
    Added a game over screen.\n\n7. Added a counter that will use the new restart
    delay. You can see it when the game over screen pops up. If that counter goes
    to 0 then the game will automatically restart.\n\n8. Added support for left and
    right arrow keys from the keyboard.\n\n\nV0.4\n\nBug Fixes\n1. Fixed a bug where
    the canvas which is responsible for displaying the UI, would sometimes be visible
    to the player.\n\n2. Fixed a bug where if you restart the game by pressing the
    restart button on the pause menu, the game would freeze and not start on its
    own after the restart.\n\n3. Fixed a bug where if you pressed the menu button
    on the pause menu and then pressed play in the main menu the game would freeze
    and not start on its own.\n\nChanges\n1. Changed the fog density to a higher
    value to make it harder for the player to see what is coming.\n\n2. Changed the
    resolution to 1920x1080 so that the game is rendered better on the main menu
    and credits page.\n\n3. Redesigned the main menu and credits page to fit the
    new resolution.\n\n4. Made 1, 2, 3, and 4 levels harder.\n\nNew\n1. Added a discord
    and Trello board icon on the main menu page that opens those links on the browser.\n\n2.
    Added a how-to-play page that will show you the controls.\n\n3. Added an early
    access splash image that will be visible while the game is loading.\n\n\nV0.3\n\nBug
    Fixes\n1. Fixed a bug that allowed the player to go off the platform and immediately
    return as nothing happened.\n\n2. Fixed a bug on the main menu that didn't allow
    the player to quit the game.\n\nChanges\n1. Updated Graphics.\n   - Changed the
    sky to something more realistic.\n   - Added reflections to more obstacles.\n\n2.
    Made all levels harder apart from 2, 8, and 10.\n\n3. Moved the finish line further
    away for all the levels and made them proportionate.\n\n4. Changed the game icon.\n\n5.
    Changed collision detection to continuous speculative for some obstacles, which
    means now they will not be affected by any force that the player applied.\n\n6.
    Optimized the game in general. Now it should take less space from your disk and
    run smoother than before.\n\nNew\n1. Added menu button to the credits screen,
    which will load the main menu screen.\n\n2. Added a pause menu screen.\n\n3.
    Added a text that displays the game version on the main menu.\n\n\nV0.2\n\nBug
    Fixes\n1. Fixed a bug that did not allow the player to proceed to level 9."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5302535af1044152a457ed104f1f4b91, type: 2}
